{"id": "tea:kaivalya-upanisad:1.1-2", "source": "src:kaivalya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.1-2"}, "paraphrase": "Āśvalāyana approaches Parameṣṭhin for the highest knowledge of Brahman; he is told to know it by faith, devotion, meditation and yoga.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "practice"], "teachers": ["tch:asvalayana", "tch:brahma"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kaivalya-upanisad:1.11", "source": "src:kaivalya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.11"}, "paraphrase": "Making the self the lower fire-stick and the praṇava the upper, by the churning of knowledge the wise burn the bond.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "practices": ["prc:pranava-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kaivalya-upanisad:1.12-14", "source": "src:kaivalya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.12-14"}, "paraphrase": "Deluded by māyā, the self in the body does everything in waking, enjoys in dream, and in deep sleep, overcome by darkness, attains happiness; from it arise the three worlds.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:turiya-turiyatita"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kaivalya-upanisad:1.16", "source": "src:kaivalya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.16"}, "paraphrase": "'That supreme Brahman, the self of all… that you are, you are that.'", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kaivalya-upanisad:1.17-23", "source": "src:kaivalya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.17-23"}, "paraphrase": "'I am subtler than the subtle, greatest; I am the manifold universe; without hands and feet, of unthinkable power; I see without eyes, hear without ears; I am to be known by all the Vedas.'", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kaivalya-upanisad:1.3", "source": "src:kaivalya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.3"}, "paraphrase": "Not by works, offspring or wealth; by renunciation alone some have reached immortality; beyond heaven, hidden in the cave, it shines, which the renouncers enter.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ethics"], "original": {"text": "na karmaṇā na prajayā dhanena tyāgenaike amṛtatvam ānaśuḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Īśādiviṃśottaraśatopaniṣadaḥ (Nirṇayasāgara collection of 120 Upaniṣads), South Indian recension carrying Upaniṣad Brahmayogin's opening maṅgala verses; e-text github.com/sanskrit/raw_etexts vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md", "licence": "text public domain; e-text licence unstated"}, "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kaivalya-upanisad:1.5-7", "source": "src:kaivalya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.5-7"}, "paraphrase": "Seated in solitude, pure, with head, neck and body straight, in the last stage of life, the renouncer meditates in the heart lotus on the Lord with Umā — three-eyed, blue-throated, tranquil.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation", "devotion"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:heart-lotus-meditation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kaivalya-upanisad:1.8-10", "source": "src:kaivalya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.8-10"}, "paraphrase": "He is Brahmā, Śiva, Indra, the imperishable, the supreme, self-luminous; he is Viṣṇu, prāṇa, time, fire and moon; seeing oneself in all beings and all beings in oneself one reaches Brahman.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:siva-visnu-identity"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kaivalya-upanisad:2", "source": "src:kaivalya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "One who recites the Śatarudrīya is purified as by fire; he resorts to Avimukta; the one beyond the stages (atyāśramin) should recite it; by this knowledge he attains kaivalya.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "karma-liberation"], "practices": ["prc:satarudriya-japa"], "concepts": ["cpt:ativarnasrami", "cpt:avimukta-taraka"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
